  "_comment": [
    "SPV mapping: which portfolio (SPV) an email means, and the banks it may name.",
    "spvs: one row per SPV. SPVNAME and SPVCODE are the registry's PRTFL_NM and PRTFL_CD; BANK is the bank the loans",
    "came from (a key of banks below); ALIASES are other ways the SPV is written. An email or attachment that writes",
    "the SPV's name, code or an alias, or names its BANK, points the request at that SPV of the customer.",
    "The same rows can be kept in spvmapping.csv instead (columns SPVNAME;SPVCODE;BANK;ALIASES, aliases separated by |);",
    "rows of both files are used.",
    "banks: how each bank may be written (aliases); Greek case endings, accents and case are ignored. flag marks the",
    "email (ERB = Eurobank)."
